{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the login's spun out again. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): The heel. It's been killing me.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Say that again? I was on the wrong screen.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Right heel. First thing when I get out of bed. Two months, every morning. Those first steps are about a seven out of ten, then I walk it off and it's alright.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She's hobbling round the kitchen every morning. I live with her, I see it.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm not hobbling. Well, a bit. I'm tired, can we just get on with it.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sore when you're just sitting?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not painful then.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Work and that?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Newsagent, on my feet all day. I run as well, or I did. No proper run in weeks, just a short one on Sundays.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): New shoes in the picture?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, uh, new runners about three months ago. It's worse in them.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Outlet pair by the servo. I told her. And that parking meter out front is going to ping us, just so you know.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any swelling round the ankle?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Numbness, pins and needles in the foot?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Pain in the knee?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the left heel?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No, not painful.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Other problems I should know? Sorry, say it again if you started, I've been logged out.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Asthma. Since I was a kid. Still got it.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): What are you using for it? Slowly, the screen's catching up.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Seratide, err, the 250, two puffs morning and night. Ventolin, two puffs if I get wheezy, not every day.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): And for the heel, any tablets?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Naproxen. 250 milligrams twice a day for a week, then I stopped. Did nothing.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She still takes a nurofen some arvos. Two tablets.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Sometimes. Yeah. Moving on.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any allergies?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fevers, or feeling crook in yourself with this?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): Has your weight changed?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, hard to say. Clothes fit the same I think. Maybe down a bit, I dunno, I haven't been on the scales.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Waterworks all ok?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. They're fine.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Now the asthma. Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Wheezing?",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. After I try to run, mostly.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke, or drink?",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): Never smoked. Couple of glasses of wine on the weekend.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Last year they did bloods and said her vitamin D was borderline. She never chased it.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, borderline. I don't have the number.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any operations?",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll just feel it. Tender on the medial side of the right heel. No swelling. And the calf's pretty tight.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): Ow. Don't. I'm over it.",
  "[SEG0050] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think we should book an ultrasound, have a look at the plantar fascia.",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She can't get off the till of a morning. It's only those first steps, then she walks it out.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): I am not waiting for a scan. If you know, say it.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): Alright, scrap the ultrasound. This sounds like plantar fasciitis. Calf and arch stretches, gel insoles from the chemist, and rest the running. if it's no better in six weeks, come back and we'll rethink."
 ],
